  "conventions": {
    "geometry": "R=1.892410005412, H=1.0459197524, w/H increases from inlet to receiver. Symmetric two-half trapped well and radially normalized sidewall; one physical carrier arm in the previously measured response. First-order prescribed f=sin\u00b2(pi w/H), cos(theta), fixed endpoints. Carrier mean intake is held fixed; the linear angular perturbation has zero mean normal rate.",
    "field": "At fixed real far baths use A, real skew B, and traction source s+i omega t with the archived quadrature normalization. Let v=A^-1(t-B A^-1 s). The coefficient of phase potential in phase with bdot is -(hbar/m) Im(conj(psi)*(v_R+i v_I))/(2|psi|\u00b2). A cos(theta) potential has section-volume-mean d_x Phi=Phi_amplitude(R)/R. This is a signed slow Eulerian carrier velocity, not an attached material mass. M_car=0.5 v^T A v; distribute diagonal terms locally and half of each gradient-link energy on each adjacent cell. Only the overall inertia is partition-independent. The dc limit is taken at fixed finite far boundaries; refine grid and box. Co-moving wall kinetic energy must correspond to material outside the counted carrier.",
    "material_bound": "Assume a positive local normal sheet mass, fully moving normally with the wall, and all archived radial mass allocated to it. Then the fraction of M_radial entering M_wall is the mass-weighted average of sin^4(pi w/H) divided by three. For nonincreasing mass density on each arm, the layer-cake representation gives a weighted average of prefix means. The prefix mean extremum is unique: derivative sign determined by t sin^4(pi t)-integral_0^t sin^4(pi x)dx, whose derivative t (sin^4(pi t))' is positive on (0,1/2) and negative on (1/2,1). Monotone class excludes the previously tested high-inertia branch. Low-mass alternatives can extend beyond the measured frequency band. Mass in the middle half above 0.542659819407 is necessary, not sufficient, for the high branch at this calibration.",
    "pressure_hypothesis": "Assume an additional material normal inertia per depth proportional to the magnitude of the prepared cycle-averaged supporting-wave radial force per depth on the sidewall (area/depth constant), frozen during the linear drive, with no additional stiffness or loss. Pressure from minus the first variation of I*omega_s with local radius. The gate radial force is summed over 0<w<H; excludes the smooth tail beyond H. Pressure weights are NOT a second copy of the scalar normal-mode inertia. Radial normalization fixes the proportionality once; it should be kept fixed for tests on other preparations. The force-based weighting has no deduction from the material action. Test by independent depth-resolved residual wall momentum under matched normal motion. Only a local, nondispersive inertia/stiffness and the previously stated selective readout over the spectral sidebands yield the predicted count."
  },
  "review": {
    "verdict": "Scoped clear for the depth-resolved carrier response, the monotone sheet-mass bound, and the one-peak prediction for pressure-proportional attachment at the stated stiffness and readout.",
    "methods": "Independent guarded direct finite-frequency quadrature and phase response, discrete linear programming extremum, and independent quarter-by-quarter central differences of translated scalar ground energies. The low-mass band-coverage test uses the existing spectral kernel.",
    "limitations": "Regional allocation convention, finite bath, radial mass assignment, sidewall-only pressure, uncalibrated local material coupling, intrinsic losses and readout. The calculation does not determine a freely translating mouth mass or a charge."
  },
